scene U: Some of the new ideas are good, and some are the same bad ideas {N} watched fail years ago under other names.
scene B: The newcomers outnumber the old hands now. Whoever leads the change will lead the group.
scene R: Part of {N} is delighted. The group has been stuck in a rut for years, and somebody finally wants to shake it.
scene G: The group is like an old hedge: it needs cutting back, not pulling up by the roots.
- W | insist that only members of long standing may vote on the change | identity | v: conformity, tradition | closed: approval: changing the rules to win; backfire: the newer members walk out | chance: 60
- U | dig out the old records and show which changes were tried before | v: universalism, security | chance: 70
