times: Nearly everyone who joins a faith as an adult, once, in the first months; about a third of US adults have left the religion they were raised in, for another or for none (Pew)
scene: {N} has been {title} for a few months, and at every gathering the others know the words, the gestures and the reasons by heart while {N} is a beat behind.
scene W: There is a right way to do this, handed down with care, and {N} wants to do it properly, not just look as if {N} belongs.
scene U: {N} keeps asking why: why this word, this order, this rule. Some of the answers are deep, and some are only habit.
scene B: {N} notices who is listened to here, and how they talk. Belief has its own pecking order.
scene R: What brought {N} here was a feeling, sudden and strong. The rules and the jargon keep getting in its way.
scene G: The others say the words without thinking, the way people speak the language they grew up in. {N} wants that ease.
- W | learn the words and the forms properly, and keep them faithfully | habit | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 80
- U | read the founding texts for yourself, from beginning to end | v: self-direction, universalism | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
- B | model yourself on the person everyone listens to | v: power, achievement | chance: 80
