- G | stop studying it and just turn up, until it soaks in | v: tradition (patience) | chance: 75
- W>U | ask for proper instruction from whoever is appointed to teach newcomers | door | v: tradition, conformity | grants: mentor | chance: 75
- U>B | learn the inner arguments well enough to hold your own with the leaders | v: power, achievement | chance: 65
- B>R | pretend to know more than you do, to be let into the exciting part sooner | v: stimulation, power | act: pretend to know more than they do, to be let into the exciting part sooner | chance: 65
- R>G | throw yourself into the next gathering with your whole heart, and see who you meet | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 80
- G>W | sit with the same old couple every week, and do what they do | habit | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 85
works: One day {N} says the words without thinking, and realises they have become {Ns} own.
works: {elder} takes {N} aside and explains the one thing the books never say.
fails: {N} gets the forms wrong in front of everyone, and the kindness that follows stings worse than a scolding.
fails: The words stay foreign, and {N} wonders whether this was a mistake.

