- W>R | apologise properly for your share, then take them out somewhere | v: benevolence, hedonism | mark: owned up | chance: 75
- U>G | compare notes on how each of your families used to argue | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 80
- B>W | agree a truce on terms that suit you, and get it said out loud | v: power, security | act: agree a truce on terms that suit them, and get it said out loud | chance: 70
- R>U | storm out for the night, and come back with a clearer head | v: self-direction | self_control: - | chance: 70
- G>B | let it go this time, and keep it in mind for the next one | v: power, security | chance: 80
works: They come through it knowing each other better, and the next argument is a little fairer.
works: By morning they are laughing about it, and something important has been settled without being said.
fails: The argument goes round in circles for days and leaves a mark on both of them.
fails: Words said that night are remembered for years.

