times: Some people with a partner, perhaps 1 in 5, once per relationship, a few years in; work is a leading reason for long-distance moves (US Census CPS)
share: .2
scene: {N} has been {title} for four years when the offer arrives: the chance of a working lifetime, in a city four hundred miles from everything {partner} has built.
scene W: {N} made promises when the two of them set up their life together, and none of the promises said anything about leaving.
scene U: {N} has made a table of it: money, careers, friends, rent, weather. It gives no answer, only a clearer question.
scene B: This is {Ns} chance. {N} has given way on {partner}'s plans before, and is not sure about giving way again.
scene R: {N} wants to go, with a hunger that is almost frightening, and does not know how to say so.
scene G: {partner} has roots here: family down the road, friends from school, a garden that took years. {N} can see what pulling them up would cost.
- W | turn it down, because the life you built together comes first | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 80
- U | set out every option on paper together, and decide only when you both agree | v: universalism, security | chance: 70
- B | take the offer, and expect them to follow once they are ready | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- R | ask them, tonight and with your whole heart, to come on the adventure | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 65
- G | stay, and look again at what this place still has to offer | v: tradition, security | chance: 65
- W>U | try six months of living apart in the week, then decide | v: self-direction, security | chance: 60
- U>B | pretend you have said yes, to force a better offer where you are | v: power, achievement | grants: inner circle at work | closed: approval: bluffing an employer; backfire: the bluff is called and both offers go | chance: 50
- B>R | take the job, and tell them you need a year on your own anyway | v: self-direction, achievement | drops: {title} | mark: moved away | chance: 75
- R>G | tell them every fear and hope you have, and decide it from the heart together | v: benevolence | chance: 75
- G>W | ask both families what they think before anything is decided | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 75
works: They make the choice together, and a year later neither of them would undo it.
works: The decision costs something, but it is the kind of cost that binds two people closer.
fails: The choice is made, and one of them carries a quiet grudge about it for years.
fails: The argument about it goes on long after the offer has gone.

