earth: you have been {title} for many years, the child needs you less every year, and there is room in your life you have not had for a long time
times: Nearly every parent, once, as the youngest child grows past ten; children need less hands-on care through the teens (estimate)
scene: {N} has been {title} for many years, and {child} needs {N} a little less every year. There is room in {Ns} life that has not been there for a long time.
scene W: {N} still keeps the old timetable in {Ns} head: pickups, meals, curfews. Half of it no longer applies.
scene U: {N} has a list of things put off for years, a course, a language, a journey, and takes it out and reads it again.
scene B: For years, most of what {N} earned went on {child}. Now some of it could go on {N}.
scene R: {N} feels a restlessness that has been asleep since before {child} came along.
scene G: The young bird is testing its wings. {N} knows the nest was always meant to empty.
- W | keep the family's rituals going, for whenever they are needed | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 75
- U | go back to studying the thing you gave up all those years ago | door | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | put money aside for yourself at last, before anyone asks for it | v: security, power | grants: savings | self_control: + | chance: 75
- R | take the journey you have dreamed of since before they came along | v: stimulation, hedonism | grants: passport | chance: 70
- G | walk the high hills alone, as you did when you were young | habit | v: universalism (nature), self-direction | body: heavy | death_if_fails: 0.002 | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 75
- W>U | volunteer to teach a class for people new to raising children | v: benevolence, universalism | grants: teaching | chance: 70
- U>B | help them take the next big step on their own, and plan the money together | v: achievement, security | chance: 70
- B>R | sell what the family has outgrown, and spend it all on yourself | v: hedonism | act: sell what the family has outgrown, and spend it all on themselves | chance: 85
- R>G | ask them along on one great journey before life takes them further away | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 60
- G>W | let them go, and keep the door open and the light on | v: tradition, benevolence | title: parent of independent adult children | chance: 75
works: The new room in {Ns} life fills with something good, and {child} seems glad of it.
works: {N} and {child} find a new footing, more like two people who choose each other's company.
fails: The space stays empty and aching, and {N} hovers more than {N} means to.
fails: {N} reaches for the old life and finds it has moved on without {N}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- senior: the one people ask, old ways and new (calls WG, s2)

== the young parents ask the old hand
tier: everyday
rate: .5
once: yes
stages: young_adult+
age: 30-105
calls: WG
holds: kind:children
tenure: 8-60
tone: joy
life: family, community
horizon: week
roles: sibling, friend, child, a neighbour
earth: you have been {title} for many years, a younger parent in the family or the street comes to you for help, and they do everything differently
times: Many experienced parents, once, after many years; experienced parents are a common source of advice for new ones (estimate)
scene: {N} has been {title} for many years and is the one the younger ones ring: {sibling}'s boy with a newborn, the couple next door, a friend whose teenager has gone silent. They do everything differently.
scene W: {N} has a proper way of doing things, learned the hard way. Half of it is now said to be wrong.
scene U: {N} is fascinated by how much the advice has changed, and how little the children have.
scene B: Being the one people ask is a kind of standing, and {N} rather likes it.
scene R: {N} sees the panic in the young faces and remembers it exactly, and wants to rush in and fix everything.
scene G: The same worries come round with every generation, like the seasons, wearing new clothes.
