- U | read up on the new methods before saying a word | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 85
- B | help, and make sure they know whom to come to next time | v: power, benevolence | grants: the one everyone asks | chance: 70
- R | turn up with a hot meal and take over for an afternoon so they can sleep | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 90
- G | tell them what nobody told you: that most of it sorts itself out | v: tradition | act: tell them what nobody ever told them: that most of it sorts itself out | chance: 70
- W>B | tell them firmly what they are doing wrong, as an elder should | v: power, conformity | mark: made an enemy | chance: 55
- U>R | ask them to teach you the new way, and try it alongside them | door | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: ask them to teach the new way, and try it alongside them | chance: 85
- B>G | offer to mind the little ones one day a week, in return for Sunday lunches | binds | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 80
- R>W | stand up for them when the rest of the family criticises their choices | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 70
- G>U | tell them about your own worst first year, and let the story teach | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 80
works: The young ones go home steadier, and {N} goes home feeling useful in a way that had been missing.
works: Old ways and new ones meet over the kitchen table, and both sides learn something.
fails: The help lands as criticism, and the young ones stop ringing for a while.
fails: {N} gives too much and is taken for granted, which stings more than expected.
